# Section A decisions on the Swagger UI verification family. Written after A1.blind was logged and the stored fields revealed.
@FG-K1-2b15ea3da2 CORRECT conf=M cls=CLASSIFICATION
why: The compound claim includes opening the Development Swagger UI and confirming it loads, and no cited policy requires that. WF-006 is limited to new apps or substantial startup changes, WF-005 to build and tests, API-016 to metadata truth, TST-010 to preserving probes. A controller change with passing tests and accurate OpenAPI JSON satisfies all four without the UI. Full entailment fails, so CANONICAL_ONLY fails. The step carries no when-clause of its own and is a DEFAULT in a knowledge skill, not a MUST. C2 allows CD for an extra trigger on the same verification duty; MIXED is not needed because all parts are one verification duty.
q: .claude/skills/swagger/SKILL.md:70-70 | open the Development Swagger UI and confirm it loads
q: .claude/skills/swagger/SKILL.md:70-70 | When API behavior changes
set classification=CANONICAL_PLUS_DELTA
set oracle_relation=PARTIALLY_ENTAILED
set strength_vs_canonical=SAME
set extra_fragment_kind=EXTRA_WORKFLOW
set extra_fragment=Open the Development Swagger UI and confirm it loads after every API behavior change (not only substantial startup changes), and exercise representative endpoints when that is a meaningful check.
set distinguishing_scenario=A controller status code changes. Build, integration tests and the OpenAPI JSON check pass, startup and composition are untouched, and the agent never opens the UI. WF-005, API-016 and TST-010 are met and WF-006 is not triggered, but K1's listed step is not done.
set trigger=API behavior changes (outer when-clause). Starting the API additionally when startup/composition changed; exercising endpoints additionally when a meaningful check.
set exceptions=NONE stated for the UI step.
set review_needed=true
set review_reason=Audit reading: the UI step is reached by the outer trigger only, because the other conditional items each carry their own when-clause. Alternative reading kept: open follows start in sequence, so only on startup changes.
alt: The run-in series could be read as start-then-open, which would limit the UI step to startup or composition changes. It would then be close to WF-006 and the claim close to CANONICAL_ONLY. The same series asks to exercise endpoints when meaningful, which also needs a running API, so running the API is not confined to startup changes. The verify skill separately covers the UI at startup (verify SKILL.md:39), so that reading would make this step redundant.
amb: Run-in sentence. Reading rests on grammar and two contextual arguments, not an explicit statement.

@FG-K1-358e1806b9 UPHOLD conf=M
why: Source says Default and uses WF-006's trigger. The Swagger UI item sits in an as-applicable list and fires only when the API exposes it. This is the startup smoke, a different clause from the API-change step at swagger SKILL.md:70.
amb: The list instantiates key composition surfaces rather than following from WF-006 by strict logic. All six candidates have this form, so it does not separate them. Stored confidence HIGH is generous; MEDIUM would be fairer, and no field was changed for that alone.

@FG-M-268251a6d0 CORRECT conf=M cls=FIELD
why: Label upheld. My blind reading was EXTRA_WORKFLOW, but C2 names an extra trigger on the same duty as CD, and WF-006's verification overlaps when the change is substantial, so CD stands. M's numbered step 4 has no condition, so the outer trigger reaches it. The stored trigger holds the skill's loading context, not the actual condition; only that field is repaired.
