@FG-M-fd05eef14c UPHOLD conf=M
why: This group's claim stops at steps 1 to 3 and does not contain the UI step, which sits in sibling FG-M-268251a6d0. CO holds for that narrower claim.
amb: Starting the API fires on any startup or composition effect, whereas WF-006 says substantial. Not separated here because the step reads as a technique detail of the same DEFAULT verification. Strength code GR here versus SL on comparable compound records in other candidates is a coding difference, not a semantic one.

@FG-M-0dcdca28e3 UPHOLD conf=M
why: Startup smoke with WF-006's trigger under an as-applicable hedge. The swagger SKILL range in its evidence belongs to the API-change step; the smoke list is the source of the claim.
amb: M's verify text has no Default marker. M reads it DEFAULT here while M1 and L0 read near-identical workflow text as MUST (PC). Equivalence with WF-006 is the same; see DRIFT_DIAGNOSTIC.

@FG-M-37676d6579 UPHOLD conf=H
why: Restates TST-010 with its exception. The swagger range only points to step 6.

@FG-M1-a876ee45ce CORRECT conf=M cls=CLASSIFICATION
why: The reach of the condition is settled from the text well enough to leave UNCERTAIN. Conditional items in this series each carry their own when-clause; this one has none. The next item (exercise endpoints when meaningful) also needs a running API, so running the API is not confined to startup changes. The verify skill separately covers the UI at startup (verify SKILL.md:56-57), which would leave this step redundant on the narrow reading. Result: DEFAULT, on every API behavior change, CD on WF-006 by extra trigger, labelled as M labels its numbered list. Source interpretation, not a human policy choice.
